{"seconds": 40.1, "exit": 0, "final": "After Rxa7+ Kd6, White has even more options. In all variations, White has a decisive advantage. The key insight is the **fork**\u2014the rook captures the pawn with check, and then the knight gives check while the bishop on g7 becomes trapped and lost.\n\n**Best move: Rxa7+**\n\n**Main line: Rxa7+ Kd8 Ne6+ Bxe6 Rxg7**\n\n**Motif: fork** (the rook and knight coordinate to trap and win the bishop)\n\n**Coaching note:**\nWhen your opponent's pieces are uncoordinated and the king is exposed, look for checks that also win material. Here, Rxa7+ captures the pawn and drives the king to an awkward square. Then Ne6+ is a follow-up check that forces Black's bishop to be sacrificed, as it's attacked twice and has no escape. The rook and knight fork the bishop and king. Whenever you see a rook and knight near an enemy king, check if they can work together to trap pieces.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Rxa7+\", \"line\": [\"Rxa7+\", \"Kd8\", \"Ne6+\", \"Bxe6\", \"Rxg7\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "5fb1/p1k3bp/1p6/6p1/R1PN4/1P1Pp2P/1P4P1/7K w - - 1 27"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "5fb1/p1k3bp/1p6/6p1/R1PN4/1P1Pp2P/1P4P1/7K w - - 1 27"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "5rb1/p1k3bp/1p6/6p1/R1PN4/1P1Pp2P/1P4P1/7K w - - 1 27"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "5rb1/p1k3bp/1p6/6p1/R1PN4/1P1Pp2P/1P4P1/7K w - - 1 27"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "5rb1/p1k3bp/1p6/6p1/R1PN4/1P1Pp2P/1P4P1/7K w - - 1 27"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "5rb1/p1k3bp/1p6/6p1/R1PN4/1P1Pp2P/1P4P1/7K w - - 1 27", "square": "d4"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "5rb1/p1k3bp/1p6/6p1/R1PN4/1P1Pp2P/1P4P1/7K w - - 1 27", "square": "a4"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-square_info", "args": {"fen": "5rb1/p1k3bp/1p6/6p1/R1PN4/1P1Pp2P/1P4P1/7K w - - 1 27", "square